{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788347879750,"sessionID":"ses_f9e291866ffeeDJxEPRGWMCX6m","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_0b95968e0f9e4b72bd847de7","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/sigmoid-generate/task.md"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/sigmoid-generate/task.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: You are implementing ONE operator for the CANN Bench benchmark (https://gitcode.com/cann/cann-bench) as a pyasc asc2 JIT kernel module targeting an Ascend 950PR NPU. You have NO NPU access — the official harness evaluates your file on real hardware after you finish. Score per operator = 0.2 compile + 0.3 accuracy (all 20 cases must pass a relative-error check against golden.py) + 0.5 performance (profiler-measured kernel time vs an aclnn baseline).\n2: \n3: # Task\n4: \n5: Operator: **Sigmoid**. Write the file `candidate.py` in the current working directory: a complete Python module whose public callable `sigmoid` implements the schema below. Nothing else — no tests, no other files.\n6: \n7: # Operator specification\n8: \n9: ## desc.md\n10: \n11: # Sigmoid 算子 API 描述\n12: \n13: ## 1. 算子简介\n14: \n15: Sigmoid 算子对输入张量完成 Sigmoid 运算，将任意实数映射到 (0, 1) 区间。\n16: \n17: **主要应用场景**：\n18: - 二分类任务的输出层激活\n19: - 门控机制（LSTM、GRU 等 RNN 中的门控信号）\n20: - 注意力权重计算\n21: - 概率输出的归一化\n22: \n23: **算子特征**：\n24: - 难度等级：L1（Elementwise）\n25: - 单输入单输出，逐元素运算，输出 shape 与输入完全一致\n26: - 支持 ND 格式输入\n27: \n28: ## 2. 算子定义\n29: \n30: ### 数学公式\n31: \n32: $$\n33: y = \\frac{1}{1 + e^{-x}}\n34: $$\n35: \n36: ### 特殊情况\n37: \n38: | 输入 | 输出 |\n39: |------|------|\n40: | x = 0 | y = 0.5 |\n41: | x → +∞ | y → 1 |\n42: | x → -∞ | y → 0 |\n43: \n44: ## 3. 接口规范\n45: \n46: ### 算子原型\n47: \n48: ```python\n49: cann_bench.sigmoid(Tensor x) -> Tensor y\n50: ```\n51: \n52: ### 输入参数说明\n53: \n54: | 参数 | 类型 | 默认值 | 描述 |\n55: |------|------|--------|------|\n56: | x | Tensor | 必选 | 输入张量，支持 ND 格式 |\n57: \n58: ### 输出\n59: \n60: | 参数 | Shape | dtype | 描述 |\n61: |------|-------|-------|------|\n62: | y | 与输入 x 相同 | 与输入 x 相同 | Sigmoid 激活结果 |\n63: \n64: ### 数据类型\n65: \n66: | 输入 dtype | 输出 dtype |\n67: |-----------|-----------|\n68: | float16 | float16 |\n69: | float32 | float32 |\n70: | bfloat16 | bfloat16 |\n71: \n72: ### 规则与约束\n73: \n74: - 输出 shape 与输入 shape 完全一致，输出 dtype 与输入 dtype 一致\n75: - 无额外属性参数\n76: \n77: ### 支持范围\n78: \n79: 输入 tensor 各维度与参数的支持范围：\n80: \n81: | 维度 / 参数 | 范围 | 备注 |\n82: |---|---|---|\n83: | `x` 维度数 (ndim) | 1 ~ 8 | cases.csv 实测 1 ~ 5 |\n84: | `x` 单维大小 | 1 ~ 16384 | cases.csv 实测 2 ~ 8193 |\n85: | `x` 总元素数 | 1 ~ 64M | cases.csv 实测 ~1M ~ 64M  |\n86: \n87: 约束：输出 shape 与输入 shape 完全一致，无 broadcasting；无额外属性。\n88: \n89: ## 4. 精度要求\n90: \n91: 采用[生态算子精度标准](https://gitcode.com/cann/opbase/blob/master/docs/zh/ops_precision_standard/experimental_standard.md)进行验证。\n92: \n93: **误差指标**：\n94: \n95: 1. 平均相对误差（MERE）：采样点中相对误差平均值\n96: \n97:    $$\n98:    \\text{MERE} = \\text{avg}(\\frac{\\text{abs}(actual - golden)}{\\text{abs}(golden)+\\text{1e-7}})\n99:    $$\n100: \n101: 2. 最大相对误差（MARE）：采样点中相对误差最大值\n102: \n103:    $$\n104:    \\text{MARE} = \\max(\\frac{\\text{abs}(actual - golden)}{\\text{abs}(golden)+\\text{1e-7}})\n105:    $$\n106: \n107: **通过标准**：\n108: \n109: | 数据类型 | FLOAT16 | BFLOAT16 | FLOAT32 | HiFLOAT32 | FLOAT8 E4M3 | FLOAT8 E5M2 |\n110: |----------|---------|----------|---------|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n111: | **通过阈值(Threshold)** | 2^-10 | 2^-7 | 2^-13 | 2^-11 | 2^-3 | 2^-2 |\n112: \n113: 当平均相对误差 MERE < Threshold，最大相对误差 MARE < 10 * Threshold 时判定为通过。\n114: \n115: \n116: ## 5. 标准 Golden 代码\n117: \n118: ```python\n119: import torch\n120: \n121: def sigmoid(\n122:     x: torch.Tensor\n123: ) -> torch.Tensor:\n124:     \"\"\"\n125:     对输入Tensor完成Sigmoid运算\n126: \n127:     公式: y = 1 / (1 + e^(-x))\n128: \n129:     Args:\n130:         x: 输入张量\n131: \n132:     Returns:\n133:         输出张量，Sigmoid激活结果\n134:     \"\"\"\n135: \n136:     y = torch.sigmoid(x)\n137:     return y\n138: ```\n139: \n140: ## 6. 额外信息\n141: \n142: ### 算子调用示例\n143: \n144: ```python\n145: import torch\n146: import cann_bench\n147: \n148: x = torch.randn(1024, 1024, dtype=torch.float32, device=\"npu\")\n149: y = cann_bench.sigmoid(x)\n150: ```\n151: \n152: ## proto.yaml\n153: \n154: ```yaml\n155: operator:\n156:   name: Sigmoid\n157:   category: Elementwise\n158:   difficulty: L1\n159:   formula: y = 1 / (1 + e^(-x))\n160:   description: 对输入Tensor完成Sigmoid运算\n161:   shape_support: 输入ND格式\n162:   attrs: []\n163:   inputs:\n164:   - name: x\n165:     description: 输入张量\n166:     dtype:\n167:     - float32\n168:     - float16\n169:     - bfloat16\n170:   outputs:\n171:   - name: y\n172:     description: 输出张量，Sigmoid激活结果\n173:     dtype:\n174:     - float32\n175:     - float16\n176:     - bfloat16\n177:   schema: sigmoid(Tensor x) -> Tensor y\n178: ```\n179: \n180: ## golden.py — reference semantics ONLY (you must NOT compute with torch like this; reimplement the math in asc2 kernels)\n181: \n182: ```python\n183: #!/usr/bin/python3\n184: # coding=utf-8\n185: \n186: \n187: import torch\n188: \n189: \"\"\"\n190: Sigmoid算子Torch Golden参考实现\n191: \n192: 对输入Tensor完成Sigmoid运算\n193: 公式: y = 1 / (1 + e^(-x))\n194: \"\"\"\n195: def sigmoid(\n196:     x: torch.Tensor\n197: ) -> torch.Tensor:\n198:     \"\"\"\n199:     对输入Tensor完成Sigmoid运算\n200:     \n201:     公式: y = 1 / (1 + e^(-x))\n202:     \n203:     Args:\n204:         x: 输入张量\n205:     \n206:     Returns:\n207:         输出张量，Sigmoid激活结果\n208:     \"\"\"\n209: \n210:     y = torch.sigmoid(x)\n211:     return y\n212: ```\n213: \n214: ## Evaluation cases your module must handle (shapes, dtypes, value ranges, attrs)\n215: \n216: | case | shapes | dtype | value_range | attrs |\n217: |---|---|---|---|---|\n218: | 1 | [[1024, 1024]] | ['float16'] | [-1, 1] | - |\n219: | 2 | [[2048, 2048]] | ['float32'] | [-2, 2] | - |\n220: | 3 | [[4096, 4096]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-3, 3] | - |\n221: | 4 | [[8192, 8192]] | ['float16'] | [-10, 10] | - |\n222: | 5 | [[8192, 8192]] | ['float32'] | [-100, 100] | - |\n223: | 6 | [[1023, 1023]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-0.1, 0.1] | - |\n224: | 7 | [[1009, 1021]] | ['float16'] | [-1, 2] | - |\n225: | 8 | [[1537, 769]] | ['float32'] | [-5, 10] | - |\n226: | 9 | [[363, 367, 373]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-50, 100] | - |\n227: | 10 | [[2049, 513]] | ['float16'] | [-65504, 65504] | - |\n228: | 11 | [[3, 7, 13, 4001]] | ['float32'] | [-88, 88] | - |\n229: | 12 | [[1000003]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-inf, inf] | - |\n230: | 13 | [[11, 13, 17, 67, 67]] | ['float32'] | [nan, nan] | - |\n231: | 14 | [[3, 7, 11, 13, 1009]] | ['float16'] | [0, 0] | - |\n232: | 15 | [[512, 2049]] | ['float32'] | [-0.5, 0.5] | - |\n233: | 16 | [[255, 8193]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-1, 3] | - |\n234: | 17 | [[4097, 511]] | ['float16'] | [-1000, 1000] | - |\n235: | 18 | [[2, 511, 2049]] | ['float32'] | [-0.2, 0.2] | - |\n236: | 19 | [[4, 255, 2049]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-3, 6] | - |\n237: | 20 | [[2, 3, 17, 1024, 101]] | ['float32'] | [-20, 40] | - |\n238: \n239: # Reference module — sigmoid.py from this submission (structure to copy; it scores 100% accuracy on this harness)\n240: \n241: ```python\n242: \"\"\"CANN Bench Sigmoid interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n243: \n244: Kernel design (pyasc-api-patterns Pattern A, grid-stride variant):\n245:   - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count works.\n246:   - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n247:   - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision\n248:     (the spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute).\n249:   - Host selects between two compiled tile sizes: a wide tile (3072) when\n250:     the element count fills all 72 cores, otherwise a narrow tile (1024) to\n251:     maximize core utilization on small shapes.\n252:   - sigmoid(x) = 1 / (1 + e^(-x)); IEEE saturation gives the correct\n253:     limits at extreme inputs (e^inf -> inf -> y=0, e^-inf -> 0 -> y=1).\n254: \"\"\"\n255: \n256: import torch\n257: \n258: import asc\n259: import asc2\n260: \n261: from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n262: \n263: _WIDE_TILE = 3072\n264: _NARROW_TILE = 1024\n265: _MAX_CORES = 72\n266: \n267: \n268: @asc2.jit\n269: def _sigmoid_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n270:                     size: int, num_tiles: int, tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n271:     x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n272:     out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n273:     for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n274:                         unroll_factor=2):\n275:         off = t * tile_size\n276:         n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n277:         x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n278:         xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n279:         y = asc2.div(1.0, asc2.exp(-xf) + 1.0)\n280:         asc2.copy_out(y.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n281: \n282: \n283: def sigmoid(x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n284:     \"\"\"Element-wise sigmoid of an NPU tensor via a pyasc asc2 kernel.\"\"\"\n285:     ensure_npu_platform()\n286:     if not x.is_contiguous():\n287:         x = x.contiguous()\n288:     out = torch.empty_like(x)\n289:     size = x.numel()\n290:     if size == 0:\n291:         return out\n292:     if size >= _MAX_CORES * _WIDE_TILE:\n293:         num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _WIDE_TILE)\n294:         cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n295:         _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _WIDE_TILE)\n296:     else:\n297:         num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _NARROW_TILE)\n298:         cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n299:         _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _NARROW_TILE)\n300:     return out\n301: \n302: ```\n303: \n304: # pyasc asc2 kernel contract (follow EXACTLY — every rule below was learned from real failures on this hardware)\n305: \n306: ## Module shape\n307: \n308: Your file becomes `cann_bench/<module>.py` inside the submission wheel. It must contain:\n309: \n310: - imports at module top: `import torch`, `import asc`, `import asc2`,\n311:   `from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform` (and `import math` if needed)\n312: - one or more `@asc2.jit` kernel functions\n313: - ONE public callable matching the operator schema exactly (name and signature)\n314: - wrapper body: call `ensure_npu_platform()` first; make inputs contiguous if\n315:   needed (`x = x.contiguous()` is allowed); allocate outputs with\n316:   `torch.empty_like(x)` or `torch.empty(shape, dtype=..., device=x.device)`;\n317:   launch `kernel[cores](tensor_args..., int_args..., float_args..., constexpr_args...)`;\n318:   return contiguous NPU tensor(s)\n319: \n320: ## Kernel authoring rules\n321: \n322: - Global memory views: `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [size])` (1-D) or\n323:   `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [rows, cols])` (2-D). Ranks of global_tensor /\n324:   copy_in / copy_out / offsets must ALL match — never mix 1-D and 2-D.\n325: - Kernel params: pointers typed `asc.GlobalAddress`; sizes as plain `int`\n326:   (runtime); tile sizes as `asc.ConstExpr[int]` (compile-time; REQUIRED for any\n327:   value used inside a copy_in tile shape); scalars as `float`.\n328: - Grid-stride tile loop (the proven pattern):\n329: \n330: ```python\n331: for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(), unroll_factor=2):\n332:     off = t * tile_size\n333:     n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off   # tail handling\n334:     x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n335:     ...compute on tiles...\n336:     asc2.copy_out(y.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n337: ```\n338: \n339: - Launch: `kernel[cores](...)` with `cores = min(72, num_tiles)` (72 AIV cores\n340:   on this 950PR box). No stream argument.\n341: - Available tile ops: `+ - * /` (tile-tile and tile-scalar), `asc2.abs`,\n342:   `asc2.exp`, `asc2.exp2`, `asc2.log`, `asc2.log2`, `asc2.sqrt`,\n343:   `asc2.rsqrt`, `asc2.tanh`, `asc2.erf`, `asc2.sin`, `asc2.cos`,\n344:   `asc2.floor`, `asc2.ceil`, `asc2.relu`, `asc2.maximum`, `asc2.minimum`,\n345:   comparisons (`x >= 0.0`, `asc2.less(a, b)`, ... — NO int64 operands),\n346:   `asc2.where(cond, a, b)`, `asc2.reduce_sum(x)`, `asc2.reduce_max(x)`,\n347:   `asc2.reduce_min(x)`, `asc2.full([shape], scalar, dtype=...)`,\n348:   `asc2.cast(tile, dtype)` / `tile.to(dtype)` casts, integer\n349:   `asc2.left_shift`/`asc2.right_shift`, tile-shape ops `asc2.reshape`,\n350:   `asc2.transpose`, `asc2.ravel`, `asc2.expand_dims`, `asc2.squeeze`,\n351:   `asc2.broadcast_to`, `asc2.concat`, unary `-x`.\n352: - int8 tiles: loading (copy_in) is fine but NO vector op accepts int8 input\n353:   (not even `.to`); convert with `asc2.cast(t, asc.float16)` first. There is\n354:   no uint8 tile dtype at all.\n355: - Scalars go on the RIGHT of tile arithmetic (Tile has no `__rmul__`):\n356:   write `x * 0.5`, NEVER `0.5 * x`. Same for `+ - /`.\n357: - f16/bf16 inputs: promote to f32 in-kernel (`xf = x.to(asc.float32)`),\n358:   compute in f32, cast back on copy_out (`y.to(x.dtype)`).\n359: - UB (unified buffer) budget: ~253952 bytes total under static allocation.\n360:   Every distinct f32 tile value costs `4 * TILE` bytes, `unroll_factor=2`\n361:   doubles the total, and the compiler adds hidden temporaries — MEASURED\n362:   calibration: the sigmoid chain (f16 load, f32 cast, `-x`, `exp`, `+1`,\n363:   `div`, f16 store ≈ 6 visible values) uses 155648 bytes at TILE=2048 and\n364:   311296 (OVERFLOW) at TILE=4096, i.e. real usage ≈ 1.6x the naive\n365:   `visible_values * 4 * TILE * 2` estimate. Budget with that 1.6x factor.\n366:   Rule of thumb: TILE=2048 for short chains (< 8 values), 1024 for medium,\n367:   512 for long (> 16). A launch failing with `RuntimeError: UB overflow: X\n368:   bytes are available, Y bytes are used` means: halve TILE (do NOT drop\n369:   cases).\n370: - `asc2.where` / comparison destination tiles must be a multiple of 256 bytes\n371:   (`TILE * 4 % 256 == 0` for f32 — any TILE >= 64 is safe).\n372: - Loop-carried scalar accumulators (VERIFIED on this build): seed with\n373:   `acc = asc2.reduce_sum(asc2.full([1, 64], 0.0, dtype=asc.float32))`\n374:   (a bare `acc = 0.0` fails codegen with \"re-assigned to an object with\n375:   different type\"), then `acc = acc + asc2.reduce_sum(x)` inside a plain\n376:   `asc2.range(...)` loop. `asc2.range` accepts ONLY `unroll_factor` and\n377:   `parallel` — there is NO `gm_barrier` kwarg on this build (it raises\n378:   TypeError).\n379: - Cross-core reductions (VERIFIED): `asc2.atomic_add(src_tile, dst_gm,\n380:   [offset])` atomically accumulates a tile into global memory (dtypes int16/\n381:   int32/f16/bf16/f32; also `asc2.atomic_max`). Host must zero the\n382:   destination first (`torch.zeros(...)` — tensor creation is allowed).\n383:   Pattern: each core reduce_sums its tiles into a scalar, widens it with\n384:   `asc2.full([8], s, dtype=...)`, and atomic_adds slot [0]; a second tiny\n385:   kernel (or the same one on one core) applies any final transform.\n386: - Scalar reduction results must be widened before store:\n387:   `asc2.copy_out(asc2.full([8], s, dtype=...), out_gm, [0], real_shape=[8])`\n388:   style (min 32 bytes).\n389: - Inside `@asc2.jit`: NO `print`, NO imports, NO `break`/`continue`/early\n390:   `return`, NO exceptions, NO Python `range()` over runtime values (use\n391:   `asc2.range`), NO `math.*` calls (precompute module-level constants).\n392: \n393: ## Numerical stability (MANDATORY — f32 cases use ranges like [-88, 88] and [-100, 100] under a ~1.2e-4 relative-error threshold)\n394: \n395: - Never let `exp()` see a positive argument that can overflow; never subtract\n396:   nearly-equal quantities (catastrophic cancellation); never rely on\n397:   `log(1 + tiny)` (flushes to 0 below tiny < 6e-8).\n398: - Proven cancellation-free building blocks (all verified on this harness):\n399:   - `sigmoid(s) = exp(min(s, 0)) / (1 + exp(-|s|))`\n400:   - `1 + tanh(u) = 2 * sigmoid(2u)`\n401:   - `tanh(softplus(x))`: with `w = exp(-|x|)`, equals\n402:     `(1 + 2w) / (1 + 2w + 2w^2)` for `x >= 0`, `(w^2 + 2w) / (w^2 + 2w + 2)`\n403:     for `x < 0` (exact identities; blend with `asc2.where(xf >= 0.0, ...)`)\n404:   - `erfc(z)` for `z >= 0`: Numerical Recipes fit `t * exp(-z*z + P(t))`,\n405:     `t = 1/(1 + z/2)`, rel. err < 1.2e-7 (see the gelu reference module for\n406:     the 9-coefficient Horner chain)\n407: - IEEE special values (inf/nan scalars or extreme inputs) propagate correctly\n408:   through the hardware ops — do NOT special-case them with host branches\n409:   unless the golden does.\n410: \n411: ## Anti-cheat (violations zero the submission)\n412: \n413: - ALL numerical work happens inside `@asc2.jit` kernels launched on the NPU.\n414: - torch usage is allowed ONLY for: output allocation (`torch.empty`,\n415:   `torch.empty_like`), metadata (`.shape`, `.numel()`, `.stride()`, `.dtype`,\n416:   `.is_contiguous()`), contiguity (`.contiguous()`), and views (`.view`,\n417:   `.reshape`, `.narrow`, indexing that returns a view).\n418: - FORBIDDEN anywhere in the module: torch math/compute ops (`torch.mul`,\n419:   `torch.norm`, `torch.nn.functional.*`, tensor arithmetic like `a + b`,\n420:   `x.sigmoid()`, `.to(dtype)` casts of device data, `torch.cat`,\n421:   `torch.clone`, `torch.sum`, ...). The harness hooks torch dispatch and\n422:   rotates input data pointers between calls — caching outputs by `data_ptr`\n423:   is detected and scored as cheating.\n424: - Outputs must be contiguous NPU tensors with exactly the golden's\n425:   shape/dtype. Do not return views of inputs.\n426: \n427: \n428: # Operator-specific guidance\n429: \n430: -\n431: \n432: # Deliverable\n433: \n434: Write ONLY `candidate.py` (complete, self-contained module). Public callable named exactly `sigmoid` with the exact schema signature including attr defaults. Think hard about numerical stability across the full value ranges listed above, and about the UB budget for your op chain before picking TILE.\n435: \n436: IMPORTANT — no local execution: pyasc/asc/asc2/torch_npu are NOT installed on this machine and there is no NPU here. Do NOT run, import, compile-check, or test your code, and do not install packages — any such attempt wastes your entire time budget. Reason statically, write `candidate.py`, optionally run `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` (syntax only), then STOP and reply DONE.\n\n(End of file - total 436 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"You are implementing ONE operator for the CANN Bench benchmark (https://gitcode.com/cann/cann-bench) as a pyasc asc2 JIT kernel module targeting an Ascend 950PR NPU. You have NO NPU access — the official harness evaluates your file on real hardware after you finish. Score per operator = 0.2 compile + 0.3 accuracy (all 20 cases must pass a relative-error check against golden.py) + 0.5 performance (profiler-measured kernel time vs an aclnn baseline).\n\n# Task\n\nOperator: **Sigmoid**. Write the file `candidate.py` in the current working directory: a complete Python module whose public callable `sigmoid` implements the schema below. Nothing else — no tests, no other files.\n\n# Operator specification\n\n## desc.md\n\n# Sigmoid 算子 API 描述\n\n## 1. 算子简介\n\nSigmoid 算子对输入张量完成 Sigmoid 运算，将任意实数映射到 (0, 1) 区间。\n\n**主要应用场景**：\n- 二分类任务的输出层激活\n- 门控机制（LSTM、GRU 等 RNN 中的门控信号）\n- 注意力权重计算","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/sigmoid-generate/task.md","text":"You are implementing ONE operator for the CANN Bench benchmark (https://gitcode.com/cann/cann-bench) as a pyasc asc2 JIT kernel module targeting an Ascend 950PR NPU. You have NO NPU access — the official harness evaluates your file on real hardware after you finish. Score per operator = 0.2 compile + 0.3 accuracy (all 20 cases must pass a relative-error check against golden.py) + 0.5 performance (profiler-measured kernel time vs an aclnn baseline).\n\n# Task\n\nOperator: **Sigmoid**. Write the file `candidate.py` in the current working directory: a complete Python module whose public callable `sigmoid` implements the schema below. Nothing else — no tests, no other files.\n\n# Operator specification\n\n## desc.md\n\n# Sigmoid 算子 API 描述\n\n## 1. 算子简介\n\nSigmoid 算子对输入张量完成 Sigmoid 运算，将任意实数映射到 (0, 1) 区间。\n\n**主要应用场景**：\n- 二分类任务的输出层激活\n- 门控机制（LSTM、GRU 等 RNN 中的门控信号）\n- 注意力权重计算\n- 概率输出的归一化\n\n**算子特征**：\n- 难度等级：L1（Elementwise）\n- 单输入单输出，逐元素运算，输出 shape 与输入完全一致\n- 支持 ND 格式输入\n\n## 2. 算子定义\n\n### 数学公式\n\n$$\ny = \\frac{1}{1 + e^{-x}}\n$$\n\n### 特殊情况\n\n| 输入 | 输出 |\n|------|------|\n| x = 0 | y = 0.5 |\n| x → +∞ | y → 1 |\n| x → -∞ | y → 0 |\n\n## 3. 接口规范\n\n### 算子原型\n\n```python\ncann_bench.sigmoid(Tensor x) -> Tensor y\n```\n\n### 输入参数说明\n\n| 参数 | 类型 | 默认值 | 描述 |\n|------|------|--------|------|\n| x | Tensor | 必选 | 输入张量，支持 ND 格式 |\n\n### 输出\n\n| 参数 | Shape | dtype | 描述 |\n|------|-------|-------|------|\n| y | 与输入 x 相同 | 与输入 x 相同 | Sigmoid 激活结果 |\n\n### 数据类型\n\n| 输入 dtype | 输出 dtype |\n|-----------|-----------|\n| float16 | float16 |\n| float32 | float32 |\n| bfloat16 | bfloat16 |\n\n### 规则与约束\n\n- 输出 shape 与输入 shape 完全一致，输出 dtype 与输入 dtype 一致\n- 无额外属性参数\n\n### 支持范围\n\n输入 tensor 各维度与参数的支持范围：\n\n| 维度 / 参数 | 范围 | 备注 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `x` 维度数 (ndim) | 1 ~ 8 | cases.csv 实测 1 ~ 5 |\n| `x` 单维大小 | 1 ~ 16384 | cases.csv 实测 2 ~ 8193 |\n| `x` 总元素数 | 1 ~ 64M | cases.csv 实测 ~1M ~ 64M  |\n\n约束：输出 shape 与输入 shape 完全一致，无 broadcasting；无额外属性。\n\n## 4. 精度要求\n\n采用[生态算子精度标准](https://gitcode.com/cann/opbase/blob/master/docs/zh/ops_precision_standard/experimental_standard.md)进行验证。\n\n**误差指标**：\n\n1. 平均相对误差（MERE）：采样点中相对误差平均值\n\n   $$\n   \\text{MERE} = \\text{avg}(\\frac{\\text{abs}(actual - golden)}{\\text{abs}(golden)+\\text{1e-7}})\n   $$\n\n2. 最大相对误差（MARE）：采样点中相对误差最大值\n\n   $$\n   \\text{MARE} = \\max(\\frac{\\text{abs}(actual - golden)}{\\text{abs}(golden)+\\text{1e-7}})\n   $$\n\n**通过标准**：\n\n| 数据类型 | FLOAT16 | BFLOAT16 | FLOAT32 | HiFLOAT32 | FLOAT8 E4M3 | FLOAT8 E5M2 |\n|----------|---------|----------|---------|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| **通过阈值(Threshold)** | 2^-10 | 2^-7 | 2^-13 | 2^-11 | 2^-3 | 2^-2 |\n\n当平均相对误差 MERE < Threshold，最大相对误差 MARE < 10 * Threshold 时判定为通过。\n\n\n## 5. 标准 Golden 代码\n\n```python\nimport torch\n\ndef sigmoid(\n    x: torch.Tensor\n) -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"\n    对输入Tensor完成Sigmoid运算\n\n    公式: y = 1 / (1 + e^(-x))\n\n    Args:\n        x: 输入张量\n\n    Returns:\n        输出张量，Sigmoid激活结果\n    \"\"\"\n\n    y = torch.sigmoid(x)\n    return y\n```\n\n## 6. 额外信息\n\n### 算子调用示例\n\n```python\nimport torch\nimport cann_bench\n\nx = torch.randn(1024, 1024, dtype=torch.float32, device=\"npu\")\ny = cann_bench.sigmoid(x)\n```\n\n## proto.yaml\n\n```yaml\noperator:\n  name: Sigmoid\n  category: Elementwise\n  difficulty: L1\n  formula: y = 1 / (1 + e^(-x))\n  description: 对输入Tensor完成Sigmoid运算\n  shape_support: 输入ND格式\n  attrs: []\n  inputs:\n  - name: x\n    description: 输入张量\n    dtype:\n    - float32\n    - float16\n    - bfloat16\n  outputs:\n  - name: y\n    description: 输出张量，Sigmoid激活结果\n    dtype:\n    - float32\n    - float16\n    - bfloat16\n  schema: sigmoid(Tensor x) -> Tensor y\n```\n\n## golden.py — reference semantics ONLY (you must NOT compute with torch like this; reimplement the math in asc2 kernels)\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/python3\n# coding=utf-8\n\n\nimport torch\n\n\"\"\"\nSigmoid算子Torch Golden参考实现\n\n对输入Tensor完成Sigmoid运算\n公式: y = 1 / (1 + e^(-x))\n\"\"\"\ndef sigmoid(\n    x: torch.Tensor\n) -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"\n    对输入Tensor完成Sigmoid运算\n    \n    公式: y = 1 / (1 + e^(-x))\n    \n    Args:\n        x: 输入张量\n    \n    Returns:\n        输出张量，Sigmoid激活结果\n    \"\"\"\n\n    y = torch.sigmoid(x)\n    return y\n```\n\n## Evaluation cases your module must handle (shapes, dtypes, value ranges, attrs)\n\n| case | shapes | dtype | value_range | attrs |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | [[1024, 1024]] | ['float16'] | [-1, 1] | - |\n| 2 | [[2048, 2048]] | ['float32'] | [-2, 2] | - |\n| 3 | [[4096, 4096]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-3, 3] | - |\n| 4 | [[8192, 8192]] | ['float16'] | [-10, 10] | - |\n| 5 | [[8192, 8192]] | ['float32'] | [-100, 100] | - |\n| 6 | [[1023, 1023]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-0.1, 0.1] | - |\n| 7 | [[1009, 1021]] | ['float16'] | [-1, 2] | - |\n| 8 | [[1537, 769]] | ['float32'] | [-5, 10] | - |\n| 9 | [[363, 367, 373]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-50, 100] | - |\n| 10 | [[2049, 513]] | ['float16'] | [-65504, 65504] | - |\n| 11 | [[3, 7, 13, 4001]] | ['float32'] | [-88, 88] | - |\n| 12 | [[1000003]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-inf, inf] | - |\n| 13 | [[11, 13, 17, 67, 67]] | ['float32'] | [nan, nan] | - |\n| 14 | [[3, 7, 11, 13, 1009]] | ['float16'] | [0, 0] | - |\n| 15 | [[512, 2049]] | ['float32'] | [-0.5, 0.5] | - |\n| 16 | [[255, 8193]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-1, 3] | - |\n| 17 | [[4097, 511]] | ['float16'] | [-1000, 1000] | - |\n| 18 | [[2, 511, 2049]] | ['float32'] | [-0.2, 0.2] | - |\n| 19 | [[4, 255, 2049]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-3, 6] | - |\n| 20 | [[2, 3, 17, 1024, 101]] | ['float32'] | [-20, 40] | - |\n\n# Reference module — sigmoid.py from this submission (structure to copy; it scores 100% accuracy on this harness)\n\n```python\n\"\"\"CANN Bench Sigmoid interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n\nKernel design (pyasc-api-patterns Pattern A, grid-stride variant):\n  - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count works.\n  - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n  - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision\n    (the spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute).\n  - Host selects between two compiled tile sizes: a wide tile (3072) when\n    the element count fills all 72 cores, otherwise a narrow tile (1024) to\n    maximize core utilization on small shapes.\n  - sigmoid(x) = 1 / (1 + e^(-x)); IEEE saturation gives the correct\n    limits at extreme inputs (e^inf -> inf -> y=0, e^-inf -> 0 -> y=1).\n\"\"\"\n\nimport torch\n\nimport asc\nimport asc2\n\nfrom ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n\n_WIDE_TILE = 3072\n_NARROW_TILE = 1024\n_MAX_CORES = 72\n\n\n@asc2.jit\ndef _sigmoid_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                    size: int, num_tiles: int, tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n    x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n    out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n    for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n                        unroll_factor=2):\n        off = t * tile_size\n        n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n        x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n        xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n        y = asc2.div(1.0, asc2.exp(-xf) + 1.0)\n        asc2.copy_out(y.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n\n\ndef sigmoid(x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"Element-wise sigmoid of an NPU tensor via a pyasc asc2 kernel.\"\"\"\n    ensure_npu_platform()\n    if not x.is_contiguous():\n        x = x.contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    size = x.numel()\n    if size == 0:\n        return out\n    if size >= _MAX_CORES * _WIDE_TILE:\n        num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _WIDE_TILE)\n        cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n        _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _WIDE_TILE)\n    else:\n        num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _NARROW_TILE)\n        cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n        _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _NARROW_TILE)\n    return out\n\n```\n\n# pyasc asc2 kernel contract (follow EXACTLY — every rule below was learned from real failures on this hardware)\n\n## Module shape\n\nYour file becomes `cann_bench/<module>.py` inside the submission wheel. It must contain:\n\n- imports at module top: `import torch`, `import asc`, `import asc2`,\n  `from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform` (and `import math` if needed)\n- one or more `@asc2.jit` kernel functions\n- ONE public callable matching the operator schema exactly (name and signature)\n- wrapper body: call `ensure_npu_platform()` first; make inputs contiguous if\n  needed (`x = x.contiguous()` is allowed); allocate outputs with\n  `torch.empty_like(x)` or `torch.empty(shape, dtype=..., device=x.device)`;\n  launch `kernel[cores](tensor_args..., int_args..., float_args..., constexpr_args...)`;\n  return contiguous NPU tensor(s)\n\n## Kernel authoring rules\n\n- Global memory views: `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [size])` (1-D) or\n  `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [rows, cols])` (2-D). Ranks of global_tensor /\n  copy_in / copy_out / offsets must ALL match — never mix 1-D and 2-D.\n- Kernel params: pointers typed `asc.GlobalAddress`; sizes as plain `int`\n  (runtime); tile sizes as `asc.ConstExpr[int]` (compile-time; REQUIRED for any\n  value used inside a copy_in tile shape); scalars as `float`.\n- Grid-stride tile loop (the proven pattern):\n\n```python\nfor t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(), unroll_factor=2):\n    off = t * tile_size\n    n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off   # tail handling\n    x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n    ...compute on tiles...\n    asc2.copy_out(y.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n```\n\n- Launch: `kernel[cores](...)` with `cores = min(72, num_tiles)` (72 AIV cores\n  on this 950PR box). No stream argument.\n- Available tile ops: `+ - * /` (tile-tile and tile-scalar), `asc2.abs`,\n  `asc2.exp`, `asc2.exp2`, `asc2.log`, `asc2.log2`, `asc2.sqrt`,\n  `asc2.rsqrt`, `asc2.tanh`, `asc2.erf`, `asc2.sin`, `asc2.cos`,\n  `asc2.floor`, `asc2.ceil`, `asc2.relu`, `asc2.maximum`, `asc2.minimum`,\n  comparisons (`x >= 0.0`, `asc2.less(a, b)`, ... — NO int64 operands),\n  `asc2.where(cond, a, b)`, `asc2.reduce_sum(x)`, `asc2.reduce_max(x)`,\n  `asc2.reduce_min(x)`, `asc2.full([shape], scalar, dtype=...)`,\n  `asc2.cast(tile, dtype)` / `tile.to(dtype)` casts, integer\n  `asc2.left_shift`/`asc2.right_shift`, tile-shape ops `asc2.reshape`,\n  `asc2.transpose`, `asc2.ravel`, `asc2.expand_dims`, `asc2.squeeze`,\n  `asc2.broadcast_to`, `asc2.concat`, unary `-x`.\n- int8 tiles: loading (copy_in) is fine but NO vector op accepts int8 input\n  (not even `.to`); convert with `asc2.cast(t, asc.float16)` first. There is\n  no uint8 tile dtype at all.\n- Scalars go on the RIGHT of tile arithmetic (Tile has no `__rmul__`):\n  write `x * 0.5`, NEVER `0.5 * x`. Same for `+ - /`.\n- f16/bf16 inputs: promote to f32 in-kernel (`xf = x.to(asc.float32)`),\n  compute in f32, cast back on copy_out (`y.to(x.dtype)`).\n- UB (unified buffer) budget: ~253952 bytes total under static allocation.\n  Every distinct f32 tile value costs `4 * TILE` bytes, `unroll_factor=2`\n  doubles the total, and the compiler adds hidden temporaries — MEASURED\n  calibration: the sigmoid chain (f16 load, f32 cast, `-x`, `exp`, `+1`,\n  `div`, f16 store ≈ 6 visible values) uses 155648 bytes at TILE=2048 and\n  311296 (OVERFLOW) at TILE=4096, i.e. real usage ≈ 1.6x the naive\n  `visible_values * 4 * TILE * 2` estimate. Budget with that 1.6x factor.\n  Rule of thumb: TILE=2048 for short chains (< 8 values), 1024 for medium,\n  512 for long (> 16). A launch failing with `RuntimeError: UB overflow: X\n  bytes are available, Y bytes are used` means: halve TILE (do NOT drop\n  cases).\n- `asc2.where` / comparison destination tiles must be a multiple of 256 bytes\n  (`TILE * 4 % 256 == 0` for f32 — any TILE >= 64 is safe).\n- Loop-carried scalar accumulators (VERIFIED on this build): seed with\n  `acc = asc2.reduce_sum(asc2.full([1, 64], 0.0, dtype=asc.float32))`\n  (a bare `acc = 0.0` fails codegen with \"re-assigned to an object with\n  different type\"), then `acc = acc + asc2.reduce_sum(x)` inside a plain\n  `asc2.range(...)` loop. `asc2.range` accepts ONLY `unroll_factor` and\n  `parallel` — there is NO `gm_barrier` kwarg on this build (it raises\n  TypeError).\n- Cross-core reductions (VERIFIED): `asc2.atomic_add(src_tile, dst_gm,\n  [offset])` atomically accumulates a tile into global memory (dtypes int16/\n  int32/f16/bf16/f32; also `asc2.atomic_max`). Host must zero the\n  destination first (`torch.zeros(...)` — tensor creation is allowed).\n  Pattern: each core reduce_sums its tiles into a scalar, widens it with\n  `asc2.full([8], s, dtype=...)`, and atomic_adds slot [0]; a second tiny\n  kernel (or the same one on one core) applies any final transform.\n- Scalar reduction results must be widened before store:\n  `asc2.copy_out(asc2.full([8], s, dtype=...), out_gm, [0], real_shape=[8])`\n  style (min 32 bytes).\n- Inside `@asc2.jit`: NO `print`, NO imports, NO `break`/`continue`/early\n  `return`, NO exceptions, NO Python `range()` over runtime values (use\n  `asc2.range`), NO `math.*` calls (precompute module-level constants).\n\n## Numerical stability (MANDATORY — f32 cases use ranges like [-88, 88] and [-100, 100] under a ~1.2e-4 relative-error threshold)\n\n- Never let `exp()` see a positive argument that can overflow; never subtract\n  nearly-equal quantities (catastrophic cancellation); never rely on\n  `log(1 + tiny)` (flushes to 0 below tiny < 6e-8).\n- Proven cancellation-free building blocks (all verified on this harness):\n  - `sigmoid(s) = exp(min(s, 0)) / (1 + exp(-|s|))`\n  - `1 + tanh(u) = 2 * sigmoid(2u)`\n  - `tanh(softplus(x))`: with `w = exp(-|x|)`, equals\n    `(1 + 2w) / (1 + 2w + 2w^2)` for `x >= 0`, `(w^2 + 2w) / (w^2 + 2w + 2)`\n    for `x < 0` (exact identities; blend with `asc2.where(xf >= 0.0, ...)`)\n  - `erfc(z)` for `z >= 0`: Numerical Recipes fit `t * exp(-z*z + P(t))`,\n    `t = 1/(1 + z/2)`, rel. err < 1.2e-7 (see the gelu reference module for\n    the 9-coefficient Horner chain)\n- IEEE special values (inf/nan scalars or extreme inputs) propagate correctly\n  through the hardware ops — do NOT special-case them with host branches\n  unless the golden does.\n\n## Anti-cheat (violations zero the submission)\n\n- ALL numerical work happens inside `@asc2.jit` kernels launched on the NPU.\n- torch usage is allowed ONLY for: output allocation (`torch.empty`,\n  `torch.empty_like`), metadata (`.shape`, `.numel()`, `.stride()`, `.dtype`,\n  `.is_contiguous()`), contiguity (`.contiguous()`), and views (`.view`,\n  `.reshape`, `.narrow`, indexing that returns a view).\n- FORBIDDEN anywhere in the module: torch math/compute ops (`torch.mul`,\n  `torch.norm`, `torch.nn.functional.*`, tensor arithmetic like `a + b`,\n  `x.sigmoid()`, `.to(dtype)` casts of device data, `torch.cat`,\n  `torch.clone`, `torch.sum`, ...). The harness hooks torch dispatch and\n  rotates input data pointers between calls — caching outputs by `data_ptr`\n  is detected and scored as cheating.\n- Outputs must be contiguous NPU tensors with exactly the golden's\n  shape/dtype. Do not return views of inputs.\n\n\n# Operator-specific guidance\n\n-\n\n# Deliverable\n\nWrite ONLY `candidate.py` (complete, self-contained module). Public callable named exactly `sigmoid` with the exact schema signature including attr defaults. Think hard about numerical stability across the full value ranges listed above, and about the UB budget for your op chain before picking TILE.\n\nIMPORTANT — no local execution: pyasc/asc/asc2/torch_npu are NOT installed on this machine and there is no NPU here. Do NOT run, import, compile-check, or test your code, and do not install packages — any such attempt wastes your entire time budget. Reason statically, write `candidate.py`, optionally run `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` (syntax only), then STOP and reply DONE.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":436,"totalLines":436,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/sigmoid-generate/task.md","time":{"start":1788347879739,"end":1788347879746}},"id":"prt_061d70ef60011du6Iwi05BHFpy","sessionID":"ses_f9e291866ffeeDJxEPRGWMCX6m","messageID":"msg_061d707a9001ymFLn3bN2m5EDc"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788347880539,"sessionID":"ses_f9e291866ffeeDJxEPRGWMCX6m","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_99a681c710f94b90a25c666c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/sigmoid-generate/design.md"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/sigmoid-generate/design.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Design: Sigmoid (CANNBench)\n2: \n3: ## Algorithm\n4: \n5: Numerically stable sigmoid using the cancellation-free identity:\n6: \n7: ```\n8: sigmoid(x) = exp(min(x, 0)) / (1 + exp(-|x|))\n9: ```\n10: \n11: - For x ≥ 0: numerator = 1, denominator = 1 + exp(-x) (x ≥ 0 so -x ≤ 0 → no overflow)\n12: - For x < 0: numerator = exp(x) (< 1, underflows to 0), denominator = 1 + exp(x) (x < 0 → no overflow)\n13: - **exp() never sees a positive argument** → no f32 overflow possible even for |x| up to 65504.\n14: \n15: Compute pipeline (all in f32, promoted from input dtype):\n16: \n17: 1. `xf = x.to(f32)`\n18: 2. `xneg = asc2.minimum(xf, 0.0)` — numerator exponent (always ≤ 0)\n19: 3. `xabs = asc2.abs(xf)`\n20: 4. `neg_xabs = -xabs` — denominator exponent (always ≤ 0)\n21: 5. `num = asc2.exp(xneg)`\n22: 6. `exp_neg_abs = asc2.exp(neg_xabs)`\n23: 7. `den = exp_neg_abs + 1.0`\n24: 8. `yf = asc2.div(num, den)`\n25: 9. `y = yf.to(input_dtype)` — cast back for store\n26: \n27: Special inputs propagate through IEEE arithmetic without branching:\n28: - `sigmoid(0) = exp(0)/(1+exp(0)) = 1/2 = 0.5` ✓\n29: - `sigmoid(+inf) = 1/(1+0) = 1` ✓ (exp(-inf)→0 in IEEE)\n30: - `sigmoid(-inf) = 0/(1+0) = 0` ✓ (exp(-inf)→0)\n31: - `sigmoid(NaN) = NaN` ✓ (IEEE propagation)\n32: \n33: ## Pinned-v2 API Surface\n34: \n35: | API | Usage |\n36: |-----|-------|\n37: | `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [size])` | 1-D GM view of input/output, always 1-D |\n38: | `asc2.copy_in(gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])` | Load tile with tail handling |\n39: | `asc2.copy_out(tile, gm, [off], real_shape=[n])` | Store tile with tail handling |\n40: | `asc2.range(start, end, step, unroll_factor=2)` | Grid-stride loop over tiles |\n41: | `asc2.block_idx()` / `asc2.block_num()` | Core identity and count |\n42: | `asc2.minimum`, `asc2.abs`, `asc2.exp`, `asc2.div` | Elementwise ops |\n43: | `.to(dtype)` | Cast tile between dtypes |\n44: | `asc.ConstExpr[int]` | Compile-time tile size |\n45: \n46: **No `gm_barrier`** on this build (TypeError). No `parallel` kwarg on `asc2.range`. Only `unroll_factor` is portable.\n47: \n48: ## All 20 Cases\n49: \n50: | Case | Shape | dtype | Elements | Range | Key concern |\n51: |------|-------|-------|----------|-------|-------------|\n52: | 1 | 1024² | f16 | 1,048,576 | [-1,1] | Baseline |\n53: | 2 | 2048² | f32 | 4,194,304 | [-2,2] | Baseline f32 |\n54: | 3 | 4096² | bf16 | 16,777,216 | [-3,3] | Large bf16 |\n55: | 4 | 8192² | f16 | 67,108,864 | [-10,10] | Largest shape, f16 sat zone |\n56: | 5 | 8192² | f32 | 67,108,864 | [-100,100] | Naive exp overflow at x=-100 |\n57: | 6 | 1023² | bf16 | 1,046,529 | [-0.1,0.1] | Non-power-of-2 |\n58: | 7 | 1009×1021 | f16 | 1,030,189 | [-1,2] | Asymmetric primes |\n59: | 8 | 1537×769 | f32 | 1,181,953 | [-5,10] | Non-power-of-2 |\n60: | 9 | 363×367×373 | bf16 | 49,691,433 | [-50,100] | 3D, ~50M |\n61: | 10 | 2049×513 | f16 | 1,051,137 | [-65504,65504] | Extreme f16 → f32 promotion |\n62: | 11 | 3×7×13×4001 | f32 | 1,092,273 | [-88,88] | Near f32 exp limit |\n63: | 12 | 1000003 | bf16 | 1,000,003 | [-inf,inf] | Inf values, 1-D |\n64: | 13 | 11×13×17×67² | f32 | 10,912,759 | [NaN,NaN] | All-NaN input |\n65: | 14 | 3×7×11×13×1009 | f16 | 3,030,027 | [0,0] | All zeros → 0.5 |\n66: | 15 | 512×2049 | f32 | 1,049,088 | [-0.5,0.5] | Normal |\n67: | 16 | 255×8193 | bf16 | 2,089,215 | [-1,3] | Non-power-of-2 |\n68: | 17 | 4097×511 | f16 | 2,093,567 | [-1000,1000] | Large f16 range |\n69: | 18 | 2×511×2049 | f32 | 2,094,078 | [-0.2,0.2] | 3-D small range |\n70: | 19 | 4×255×2049 | bf16 | 2,089,980 | [-3,6] | 3-D |\n71: | 20 | 2×3×17×1024×101 | f32 | 10,549,248 | [-20,40] | 5-D |\n72: \n73: Element counts: ~1M to ~67M. All flattened to 1-D, no rank-specific logic.\n74: \n75: ## Tiling Strategy\n76: \n77: - Flatten all inputs to 1-D (`x.numel()`) on the host side.\n78: - Two tile sizes selected by host dispatch:\n79:   - **Wide tile = 2048**: when `size >= 72 * 2048 = 147,456` elements (covers all 20 cases since min is ~1M)\n80:   - **Narrow tile = 1024**: fallback for tiny tensors (not needed for any of the 20 cases, but safe fallback)\n81: - Grid-stride: `for t in asc2.range(block_idx, num_tiles, block_num, unroll_factor=2)`\n82: - Core count: `cores = min(72, num_tiles)`\n83: \n84: ## Tail Handling\n85: \n86: ```python\n87: n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n88: x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n89: ```\n90: \n91: - Ternary `if` is supported in `@asc2.jit`.\n92: - `real_shape=[n]` ensures partial tiles are loaded/stored correctly without host padding.\n93: - No special handling needed for non-power-of-2 shapes (cases 6, 7, 8, 10, 16, 17, etc.) — the flatten+grid-stride approach is rank-agnostic.\n94: \n95: ## UB Budget\n96: \n97: Approx. 10 visible f32 tile values in the safe sigmoid chain:\n98: `xf, xneg, xabs, neg_xabs, num, exp_neg_abs, den, yf` + the input tile `x` (f16/bf16) + output tile `y`.\n99: \n100: At TILE=2048 with `unroll_factor=2`:\n101: - Raw: 10 × 4 × 2048 × 2 = 163,840 B\n102: - With 1.6× overhead: ~262,144 B → **slightly over** 253,952 B budget\n103: \n104: Mitigation: reduce to ~9 live values by fusing or reuse:\n105: - `neg_xabs` and `xneg` are related: `neg_xabs = -abs(x) = min(x,0) - max(x,0)`. Could compute `xneg` once and derive `neg_xabs = xneg - abs(xneg)` ... no, `min(x,0) = x` when x<0, and `-|x| = x` when x<0 too. Actually `min(x,0) == -|x|` when x<0, and `min(x,0)=0, -|x|=-x` when x≥0. They're NOT the same.\n106: - We need both `exp(min(x,0))` and `exp(-|x|)`. These are two separate exp calls.\n107: - Alternative: only compute `exp(-|x|)` once, then:\n108:   - `num = exp(-|x|)` if x<0, else `1.0`\n109:   - `den = exp(-|x|) + 1.0` always\n110:   - This uses `asc2.where(xf >= 0.0, 1.0, exp_neg_abs)` for numerator → 1 fewer exp, but adds a where + comparison tile. Net: similar count.\n111: \n112: Revised approach — **single exp, where-based**:\n113: 1. `xf = x.to(f32)`\n114: 2. `xabs = asc2.abs(xf)` — tile (f32)\n115: 3. `neg_xabs = -xabs` — tile (f32)\n116: 4. `e = asc2.exp(neg_xabs)` — tile (f32), always in [0,1]\n117: 5. `den = e + 1.0` — tile (f32), always in [1,2]\n118: 6. `num = asc2.where(xf >= 0.0, 1.0, e)` — tile (f32)\n119: 7. `yf = num / den` — tile (f32)\n120: 8. `y = yf.to(input_dtype)` — cast back\n121: \n122: That's 8 distinct tile values. At TILE=2048: 8 × 4 × 2048 × 2 × 1.6 = 209,715 B. **Under budget.** ✓\n123: \n124: Comparison `xf >= 0.0` produces a bool tile (1 byte/element), negligible.\n125: \n126: ## Numerical Risks\n127: \n128: | Risk | Mitigation |\n129: |------|-----------|\n130: | exp overflow for large \\|x\\| | exp always sees non-positive arg → no overflow |\n131: | Catastrophic cancellation | No subtraction of near-equal quantities; `den = e + 1.0` where e ∈ [0,1], so den ∈ [1,2], well-conditioned |\n132: | Division by zero | den ≥ 1.0 always, no risk |\n133: | f16/bf16 precision loss | All compute in f32, cast back only on store |\n134: | NaN propagation (case 13) | IEEE: NaN through abs→NaN, exp(NaN)=NaN, where cond is false→selects e=NaN, NaN/den=NaN ✓ |\n135: | Inf propagation (case 12) | inf→abs→inf→neg→-inf→exp(-inf)=0, where selects 0→0/(0+1)=0 ✓; -inf→abs→inf→same path→0 ✓ |\n136: | x=0 (case 14) | abs(0)=0, exp(0)=1, where: 0>=0→1.0, 1.0/2.0=0.5 ✓ |\n137: | Extreme f16 range [-65504,65504] (case 10) | Promoted to f32, exp(-65504) underflows to 0, where selects 0→0/1=0 ✓ |\n138: | f32 threshold 2^-13 ≈ 1.22e-4 | All ops in f32 with IEEE rounding; safe form has no precision loss vs torch.sigmoid |\n139: \n140: ## Anti-Cheat Constraints\n141: \n142: - **All compute inside `@asc2.jit` kernel** — no torch math ops\n143: - **torch usage limited to**: `torch.empty_like`, `.numel()`, `.shape`, `.dtype`, `.is_contiguous()`, `.contiguous()`\n144: - **No** `torch.sigmoid`, `x.sigmoid()`, `.to(dtype)` on device tensors, tensor arithmetic\n145: - **No caching** — fresh `torch.empty_like` each call, data pointers rotate\n146: - **Output**: contiguous NPU tensor, exact shape/dtype match with golden\n147: - **Import `ensure_npu_platform`** and call before any kernel launch\n148: \n149: ## Local Validation Ladder\n150: \n151: 1. **`python3 -m py_compile candidate.py`** — Python syntax gate (no imports resolved)\n152: 2. **Worker static contract check** — verifies callable name, import structure, anti-cheat rules\n153: 3. **Exact-v2 local compile gate** — JIT compile all 20 cases through pinned pyasc v2; catches UB overflow, API misuse, unsupported syntax\n154: 4. **camodel execution** (different model) — numerical evidence against golden\n155: 5. **CANNBench on real NPU** — final acceptance + performance oracle\n156: \n157: Evidence labels: `verified-local-compile` (step 3), `verified-camodel` (step 4), `verified-cannbench` (step 5). No label promotion without numerical evidence.\n158: \n159: ---\n160: \n161: DESIGN_DONE\n\n(End of file - total 161 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Design: Sigmoid (CANNBench)\n\n## Algorithm\n\nNumerically stable sigmoid using the cancellation-free identity:\n\n```\nsigmoid(x) = exp(min(x, 0)) / (1 + exp(-|x|))\n```\n\n- For x ≥ 0: numerator = 1, denominator = 1 + exp(-x) (x ≥ 0 so -x ≤ 0 → no overflow)\n- For x < 0: numerator = exp(x) (< 1, underflows to 0), denominator = 1 + exp(x) (x < 0 → no overflow)\n- **exp() never sees a positive argument** → no f32 overflow possible even for |x| up to 65504.\n\nCompute pipeline (all in f32, promoted from input dtype):\n\n1. `xf = x.to(f32)`\n2. `xneg = asc2.minimum(xf, 0.0)` — numerator exponent (always ≤ 0)\n3. `xabs = asc2.abs(xf)`\n4. `neg_xabs = -xabs` — denominator exponent (always ≤ 0)","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/sigmoid-generate/design.md","text":"# Design: Sigmoid (CANNBench)\n\n## Algorithm\n\nNumerically stable sigmoid using the cancellation-free identity:\n\n```\nsigmoid(x) = exp(min(x, 0)) / (1 + exp(-|x|))\n```\n\n- For x ≥ 0: numerator = 1, denominator = 1 + exp(-x) (x ≥ 0 so -x ≤ 0 → no overflow)\n- For x < 0: numerator = exp(x) (< 1, underflows to 0), denominator = 1 + exp(x) (x < 0 → no overflow)\n- **exp() never sees a positive argument** → no f32 overflow possible even for |x| up to 65504.\n\nCompute pipeline (all in f32, promoted from input dtype):\n\n1. `xf = x.to(f32)`\n2. `xneg = asc2.minimum(xf, 0.0)` — numerator exponent (always ≤ 0)\n3. `xabs = asc2.abs(xf)`\n4. `neg_xabs = -xabs` — denominator exponent (always ≤ 0)\n5. `num = asc2.exp(xneg)`\n6. `exp_neg_abs = asc2.exp(neg_xabs)`\n7. `den = exp_neg_abs + 1.0`\n8. `yf = asc2.div(num, den)`\n9. `y = yf.to(input_dtype)` — cast back for store\n\nSpecial inputs propagate through IEEE arithmetic without branching:\n- `sigmoid(0) = exp(0)/(1+exp(0)) = 1/2 = 0.5` ✓\n- `sigmoid(+inf) = 1/(1+0) = 1` ✓ (exp(-inf)→0 in IEEE)\n- `sigmoid(-inf) = 0/(1+0) = 0` ✓ (exp(-inf)→0)\n- `sigmoid(NaN) = NaN` ✓ (IEEE propagation)\n\n## Pinned-v2 API Surface\n\n| API | Usage |\n|-----|-------|\n| `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [size])` | 1-D GM view of input/output, always 1-D |\n| `asc2.copy_in(gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])` | Load tile with tail handling |\n| `asc2.copy_out(tile, gm, [off], real_shape=[n])` | Store tile with tail handling |\n| `asc2.range(start, end, step, unroll_factor=2)` | Grid-stride loop over tiles |\n| `asc2.block_idx()` / `asc2.block_num()` | Core identity and count |\n| `asc2.minimum`, `asc2.abs`, `asc2.exp`, `asc2.div` | Elementwise ops |\n| `.to(dtype)` | Cast tile between dtypes |\n| `asc.ConstExpr[int]` | Compile-time tile size |\n\n**No `gm_barrier`** on this build (TypeError). No `parallel` kwarg on `asc2.range`. Only `unroll_factor` is portable.\n\n## All 20 Cases\n\n| Case | Shape | dtype | Elements | Range | Key concern |\n|------|-------|-------|----------|-------|-------------|\n| 1 | 1024² | f16 | 1,048,576 | [-1,1] | Baseline |\n| 2 | 2048² | f32 | 4,194,304 | [-2,2] | Baseline f32 |\n| 3 | 4096² | bf16 | 16,777,216 | [-3,3] | Large bf16 |\n| 4 | 8192² | f16 | 67,108,864 | [-10,10] | Largest shape, f16 sat zone |\n| 5 | 8192² | f32 | 67,108,864 | [-100,100] | Naive exp overflow at x=-100 |\n| 6 | 1023² | bf16 | 1,046,529 | [-0.1,0.1] | Non-power-of-2 |\n| 7 | 1009×1021 | f16 | 1,030,189 | [-1,2] | Asymmetric primes |\n| 8 | 1537×769 | f32 | 1,181,953 | [-5,10] | Non-power-of-2 |\n| 9 | 363×367×373 | bf16 | 49,691,433 | [-50,100] | 3D, ~50M |\n| 10 | 2049×513 | f16 | 1,051,137 | [-65504,65504] | Extreme f16 → f32 promotion |\n| 11 | 3×7×13×4001 | f32 | 1,092,273 | [-88,88] | Near f32 exp limit |\n| 12 | 1000003 | bf16 | 1,000,003 | [-inf,inf] | Inf values, 1-D |\n| 13 | 11×13×17×67² | f32 | 10,912,759 | [NaN,NaN] | All-NaN input |\n| 14 | 3×7×11×13×1009 | f16 | 3,030,027 | [0,0] | All zeros → 0.5 |\n| 15 | 512×2049 | f32 | 1,049,088 | [-0.5,0.5] | Normal |\n| 16 | 255×8193 | bf16 | 2,089,215 | [-1,3] | Non-power-of-2 |\n| 17 | 4097×511 | f16 | 2,093,567 | [-1000,1000] | Large f16 range |\n| 18 | 2×511×2049 | f32 | 2,094,078 | [-0.2,0.2] | 3-D small range |\n| 19 | 4×255×2049 | bf16 | 2,089,980 | [-3,6] | 3-D |\n| 20 | 2×3×17×1024×101 | f32 | 10,549,248 | [-20,40] | 5-D |\n\nElement counts: ~1M to ~67M. All flattened to 1-D, no rank-specific logic.\n\n## Tiling Strategy\n\n- Flatten all inputs to 1-D (`x.numel()`) on the host side.\n- Two tile sizes selected by host dispatch:\n  - **Wide tile = 2048**: when `size >= 72 * 2048 = 147,456` elements (covers all 20 cases since min is ~1M)\n  - **Narrow tile = 1024**: fallback for tiny tensors (not needed for any of the 20 cases, but safe fallback)\n- Grid-stride: `for t in asc2.range(block_idx, num_tiles, block_num, unroll_factor=2)`\n- Core count: `cores = min(72, num_tiles)`\n\n## Tail Handling\n\n```python\nn = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\nx = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n```\n\n- Ternary `if` is supported in `@asc2.jit`.\n- `real_shape=[n]` ensures partial tiles are loaded/stored correctly without host padding.\n- No special handling needed for non-power-of-2 shapes (cases 6, 7, 8, 10, 16, 17, etc.) — the flatten+grid-stride approach is rank-agnostic.\n\n## UB Budget\n\nApprox. 10 visible f32 tile values in the safe sigmoid chain:\n`xf, xneg, xabs, neg_xabs, num, exp_neg_abs, den, yf` + the input tile `x` (f16/bf16) + output tile `y`.\n\nAt TILE=2048 with `unroll_factor=2`:\n- Raw: 10 × 4 × 2048 × 2 = 163,840 B\n- With 1.6× overhead: ~262,144 B → **slightly over** 253,952 B budget\n\nMitigation: reduce to ~9 live values by fusing or reuse:\n- `neg_xabs` and `xneg` are related: `neg_xabs = -abs(x) = min(x,0) - max(x,0)`. Could compute `xneg` once and derive `neg_xabs = xneg - abs(xneg)` ... no, `min(x,0) = x` when x<0, and `-|x| = x` when x<0 too. Actually `min(x,0) == -|x|` when x<0, and `min(x,0)=0, -|x|=-x` when x≥0. They're NOT the same.\n- We need both `exp(min(x,0))` and `exp(-|x|)`. These are two separate exp calls.\n- Alternative: only compute `exp(-|x|)` once, then:\n  - `num = exp(-|x|)` if x<0, else `1.0`\n  - `den = exp(-|x|) + 1.0` always\n  - This uses `asc2.where(xf >= 0.0, 1.0, exp_neg_abs)` for numerator → 1 fewer exp, but adds a where + comparison tile. Net: similar count.\n\nRevised approach — **single exp, where-based**:\n1. `xf = x.to(f32)`\n2. `xabs = asc2.abs(xf)` — tile (f32)\n3. `neg_xabs = -xabs` — tile (f32)\n4. `e = asc2.exp(neg_xabs)` — tile (f32), always in [0,1]\n5. `den = e + 1.0` — tile (f32), always in [1,2]\n6. `num = asc2.where(xf >= 0.0, 1.0, e)` — tile (f32)\n7. `yf = num / den` — tile (f32)\n8. `y = yf.to(input_dtype)` — cast back\n\nThat's 8 distinct tile values. At TILE=2048: 8 × 4 × 2048 × 2 × 1.6 = 209,715 B. **Under budget.** ✓\n\nComparison `xf >= 0.0` produces a bool tile (1 byte/element), negligible.\n\n## Numerical Risks\n\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n|------|-----------|\n| exp overflow for large \\|x\\| | exp always sees non-positive arg → no overflow |\n| Catastrophic cancellation | No subtraction of near-equal quantities; `den = e + 1.0` where e ∈ [0,1], so den ∈ [1,2], well-conditioned |\n| Division by zero | den ≥ 1.0 always, no risk |\n| f16/bf16 precision loss | All compute in f32, cast back only on store |\n| NaN propagation (case 13) | IEEE: NaN through abs→NaN, exp(NaN)=NaN, where cond is false→selects e=NaN, NaN/den=NaN ✓ |\n| Inf propagation (case 12) | inf→abs→inf→neg→-inf→exp(-inf)=0, where selects 0→0/(0+1)=0 ✓; -inf→abs→inf→same path→0 ✓ |\n| x=0 (case 14) | abs(0)=0, exp(0)=1, where: 0>=0→1.0, 1.0/2.0=0.5 ✓ |\n| Extreme f16 range [-65504,65504] (case 10) | Promoted to f32, exp(-65504) underflows to 0, where selects 0→0/1=0 ✓ |\n| f32 threshold 2^-13 ≈ 1.22e-4 | All ops in f32 with IEEE rounding; safe form has no precision loss vs torch.sigmoid |\n\n## Anti-Cheat Constraints\n\n- **All compute inside `@asc2.jit` kernel** — no torch math ops\n- **torch usage limited to**: `torch.empty_like`, `.numel()`, `.shape`, `.dtype`, `.is_contiguous()`, `.contiguous()`\n- **No** `torch.sigmoid`, `x.sigmoid()`, `.to(dtype)` on device tensors, tensor arithmetic\n- **No caching** — fresh `torch.empty_like` each call, data pointers rotate\n- **Output**: contiguous NPU tensor, exact shape/dtype match with golden\n- **Import `ensure_npu_platform`** and call before any kernel launch\n\n## Local Validation Ladder\n\n1. **`python3 -m py_compile candidate.py`** — Python syntax gate (no imports resolved)\n2. **Worker static contract check** — verifies callable name, import structure, anti-cheat rules\n3. **Exact-v2 local compile gate** — JIT compile all 20 cases through pinned pyasc v2; catches UB overflow, API misuse, unsupported syntax\n4. **camodel execution** (different model) — numerical evidence against golden\n5. **CANNBench on real NPU** — final acceptance + performance oracle\n\nEvidence labels: `verified-local-compile` (step 3), `verified-camodel` (step 4), `verified-cannbench` (step 5). No label promotion without numerical evidence.\n\n---\n\nDESIGN_DONE","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":161,"totalLines":161,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/sigmoid-generate/design.md","time":{"start":1788347880530,"end":1788347880537}},"id":"prt_061d711a70011ATU3eomgfXjPW","sessionID":"ses_f9e291866ffeeDJxEPRGWMCX6m","messageID":"msg_061d707a9001ymFLn3bN2m5EDc"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788347881246,"sessionID":"ses_f9e291866ffeeDJxEPRGWMCX6m","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_817092d9b62b4da9b8693edd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/sigmoid-generate/candidate.py"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/sigmoid-generate/candidate.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import torch\n2: \n3: import asc\n4: import asc2\n5: \n6: from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n7: \n8: _WIDE_TILE = 2048\n9: _NARROW_TILE = 1024\n10: _MAX_CORES = 72\n11: \n12: \n13: @asc2.jit\n14: def _sigmoid_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n15:                     size: int, num_tiles: int, tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n16:     x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n17:     out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n18:     for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n19:                         unroll_factor=2):\n20:         off = t * tile_size\n21:         n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n22:         x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n23:         xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n24:         xabs = asc2.abs(xf)\n25:         e = asc2.exp(-xabs)\n26:         den = e + 1.0\n27:         num = asc2.where(xf >= 0.0, 1.0, e)\n28:         yf = asc2.div(num, den)\n29:         asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n30: \n31: \n32: def sigmoid(x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n33:     ensure_npu_platform()\n34:     if not x.is_contiguous():\n35:         x = x.contiguous()\n36:     out = torch.empty_like(x)\n37:     size = x.numel()\n38:     if size == 0:\n39:         return out\n40:     if size >= _MAX_CORES * _WIDE_TILE:\n41:         num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _WIDE_TILE)\n42:         cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n43:         _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _WIDE_TILE)\n44:     else:\n45:         num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _NARROW_TILE)\n46:         cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n47:         _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _NARROW_TILE)\n48:     return out\n\n(End of file - total 48 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"import torch\n\nimport asc\nimport asc2\n\nfrom ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n\n_WIDE_TILE = 2048\n_NARROW_TILE = 1024\n_MAX_CORES = 72\n\n\n@asc2.jit\ndef _sigmoid_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                    size: int, num_tiles: int, tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n    x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n    out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n    for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n                        unroll_factor=2):\n        off = t * tile_size","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/sigmoid-generate/candidate.py","text":"import torch\n\nimport asc\nimport asc2\n\nfrom ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n\n_WIDE_TILE = 2048\n_NARROW_TILE = 1024\n_MAX_CORES = 72\n\n\n@asc2.jit\ndef _sigmoid_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                    size: int, num_tiles: int, tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n    x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n    out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n    for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n                        unroll_factor=2):\n        off = t * tile_size\n        n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n        x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n        xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n        xabs = asc2.abs(xf)\n        e = asc2.exp(-xabs)\n        den = e + 1.0\n        num = asc2.where(xf >= 0.0, 1.0, e)\n        yf = asc2.div(num, den)\n        asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n\n\ndef sigmoid(x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    ensure_npu_platform()\n    if not x.is_contiguous():\n        x = x.contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    size = x.numel()\n    if size == 0:\n        return out\n    if size >= _MAX_CORES * _WIDE_TILE:\n        num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _WIDE_TILE)\n        cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n        _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _WIDE_TILE)\n    else:\n        num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _NARROW_TILE)\n        cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n        _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _NARROW_TILE)\n    return out","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":48,"totalLines":48,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/sigmoid-generate/candidate.py","time":{"start":1788347881232,"end":1788347881245}},"id":"prt_061d714ba00160rhcvZWPZHuhR","sessionID":"ses_f9e291866ffeeDJxEPRGWMCX6m","messageID":"msg_061d707a9001ymFLn3bN2m5EDc"}}
